WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.064
In Yuan times, a red curtain hung over the stage and the seats below were full of people who loved the theatre. Amid drums and gongs, a fine play was about to begin.

00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:18.494
There was a playwright in his fifties named Guan Hanqing, writing his script with full concentration by lamplight.

00:00:18.844 --> 00:00:30.508
His brush flew quickly across the paper, and a moving story slowly appeared. He wanted to write all the injustices of the world into his plays.

00:00:30.858 --> 00:00:34.578
When he reached the most moving parts, his own eyes grew wet too.

00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:40.928
The heroine of the story is a young woman named Dou E; she is kind-hearted and strong.

00:00:41.278 --> 00:00:44.878
The moment the audience saw her, their hearts ached for her.

00:00:45.228 --> 00:00:51.060
But a villain framed her, the officials judged her guilty, and she suffered a terrible injustice.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:01:01.562
The Injustice to Dou E moved countless audiences and became the most famous masterpiece of Yuan drama. Even today, people still pass this story on.

